        "content": "<p>I was looking through the elliptic curve code in mathlib and I came across this horrible thing in the trace of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing.mk_XYIdeal%27_mul_mk_XYIdeal%27#doc\">docs#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing.mk_XYIdeal'_mul_mk_XYIdeal'</a> :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">7585528.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalCommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocCommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalCommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocCommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNonUnitalNonAssocSemiring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>That is a <em>lot</em> of heartbeats to spend failing to check that two AddCommMonoid instances are equal. I suspected that there was a diamond, but it seems to me that what is actually going on is that both of these are <code>AddCommMonoid</code> instances on <code>FunctionField ?m.19</code> where <code>?m.19 : Affine ?m.17</code> and <code>?m.17 : Type ?u.85143</code>. Things get unfolded and unfolded and unfolded into smaller and smaller failures such as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">203689.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">12</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddSemigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAddSemigroup</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where <code>?m.12 : Field (FunctionField ?m.19)</code> and at the very end of all of the many paths, Lean bails out with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">synthInstance</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">15575.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">💥️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FunctionField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">19</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Should this be happening? This is all going on in</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">definition</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">header</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">27570253.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WeierstrassCurve</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Affine</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk_XYIdeal'_mul_mk_XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and that 27M is 3*9M where each 9M is an instance of the horrible things above.</p>\n<p>Here is where things seem to go off the rails in the trace:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">8511026.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FunctionField</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">8510930.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FunctionField</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▼</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">whnf</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">14.000000</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Non</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">easy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">whnf</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=