    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110038\">@Kevin Buzzard</span> beyond having found a solution, do you understand now why inserting <code>W</code> three times helps so much?</p>",
        "id": 596913550,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1779427959
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>All I understand is this: those questions in the typeclass inference trace have positive answers if you use the correct metavariables. Somehow the algorithm doesn't assign the metavariables until too late, and by this point an expensive failure has occurred.</p>",
        "id": 596917464,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779429795
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a MWE if you want to play around. The <code>#check</code> takes 5 times as long to succeed if <code>W</code> is not given explicitly, despite the fact that <code>W</code> can be inferred from <code>h</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AlgebraicGeometry</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">EllipticCurve</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Affine</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Point</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WeierstrassCurve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Affine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">useHeartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nonsingular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ClassGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- [Elab.command] [8115478.000000] ✅️ #check ClassGroup.mk (XYIdeal' h₁) ▶</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">useHeartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nonsingular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ClassGroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- [Elab.command] [1614213.000000] ✅️ #check ClassGroup.mk (XYIdeal' (W := W) h₁) ▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The expensive defeq failure (which shouldn't fail in my mental model of things) is here:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FunctionField</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">XYIdeal'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">5967116</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">❌️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                                </span><span class=\"bp\">=?=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FractionalIdeal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">CoordinateRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">19</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⁰</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FunctionField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">19</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and <code>?m.19</code> is still unassigned, presumably because of some higher order unification failure or something. I asked a language model but I absolutely cannot endorse the response below, this is just the kind of situation where it speaks confidently about something I don't understand properly so this might be absolute nonsense.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That single isDefEq is 5.97M heartbeats — basically the whole cost. The synthInstance calls for Field (FunctionField ?m.19) are <em>children</em> of it. So this is a <strong>unification</strong> problem, and ?m.19</p>\n<p>is XYIdeal''s implicit W, <strong>still unassigned</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Why W is unassigned at that point</strong></p>\n<p>This isDefEq is <strong>expected-type propagation</strong>. When the elaborator processes XYIdeal' h₁, it does <em>not</em> elaborate the explicit argument first. It:</p>\n<p>1. instantiates XYIdeal''s implicits as metavariables → ?m.19 for W, result type (FractionalIdeal (CoordinateRing ?m.19)⁰ (FunctionField ?m.19))ˣ;</p>\n<p>2. <strong>propagates the expected type</strong>: unifies that result type against the slot it's going into — ClassGroup.mk's argument type (FractionalIdeal ?m.9⁰ ?m.10)ˣ;</p>\n<p>3. <em>only then</em> elaborates the explicit argument h₁.</p>\n<p>Step 2 is the monster isDefEq, and it runs <strong>before</strong> step 3. The catch — and the real answer to your question:</p>\n<p><strong>W</strong> <strong>is only readable from</strong> <strong>h₁ : W.Nonsingular x y</strong><strong>, which is the explicit argument, processed last. The expected type from</strong> <strong>ClassGroup.mk</strong> <strong>is</strong> <strong>(FractionalIdeal ?m.9⁰ ?m.10)ˣ</strong> <strong>—</strong> <strong><em>entirely</em></strong> </p>\n<p><strong><em>metavariables</em></strong> <strong>(<em><strong><em><a href=\"http://ClassGroup.mk\">ClassGroup.mk</a></em></strong></em>'s own</strong> <strong>R<em><strong><em>/</em></strong></em>K</strong> <strong>are themselves unsolved). So there is nothing concrete anywhere for</strong> <strong>W</strong> <strong>to unify against until</strong> <strong>h₁</strong> <strong>is reached.</strong> Lean isn't \"failing to unify sooner\" —</p>\n<p>there is genuinely no information to unify W with until the explicit argument, yet a heavy unification is forced before it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This might be an argument for making more of the inputs to <code>ClassGroup.mk</code> explicit.</p>",
        "id": 596924016,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779432738
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I asked Jovan Gerbschied (who I trust a darn sight more than Claude when it comes to the typeclass algorithm) for an explanation. My understanding of his answer is that Claude did explain the algorithm correctly: when attempting to typecheck <code>ClassGroup.mk (XYIdeal' h)</code> Lean first makes metavariables for <code>R</code> and <code>K</code> (the inputs to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ClassGroup.mk#doc\">docs#ClassGroup.mk</a> ) and then reads <code>XYIdeal'</code> as far as <code>h</code> and then stops before reading <code>h</code> (the first explicit input to <code>XYIdeal'</code>) and attempts to unify the type of what <code>ClassGroup.mk</code> is eating and what <code>XYIdeal' _</code> is providing, and apparently this is usually a good idea but here it isn't.</p>\n<p>I think a more principled solution is to make <code>ClassGroup.mk</code> take <code>K</code> explicitly (and perhaps even <code>R</code> too) and this is what I tried in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39685\">#39685</a> -- now we don't need <code>(W := W)</code>, we can just supply the function field instead (I thought it was pretty weird with <code>ClassGroup.mk</code> having no explicit inputs).</p>",
        "id": 597396048,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779625238
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, I'll have a look and try to digest all this. But for your last point, having to provide R seems strange since this should really be easy to infer from an <code>Ideal R</code>, no?</p>",
        "id": 597682668,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1779740838
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The point is that the unification is taking place before lean looks at h.</p>",
        "id": 597683781,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779741512
    }
]